==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
15th century, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|fidélité|lang=fr}} from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|fidelitas|fidēlitās|lang=la}}, from {{term|fidelis|fidēlis|faithful|lang=la}}, from {{term|fides|fidēs|faith, loyalty|lang=la}} (English {{term|faith|lang=en}}), from {{proto|ine-pro|bʰidʰ-|lang=en}}, [[zero-grade]] of {{proto|ine-pro|bʰeydʰ-|to command, to persuade, to trust|lang=en}} (English {{term|bide|lang=en}}).

===Noun===
{{en-noun|fidelities}}

# [[faithfulness]] to one's [[duties]]
# [[accuracy]], or exact [[correspondence]] to some given [[quality]] or [[fact]]
# [[loyalty]], especially to one's [[spouse]]
# the [[degree]] to which a [[system]] accurately [[reproduce]]s an input.

